A loop that never ends is stopped, and the scripts keep working after it: a
terminal has no Ctrl+Break, mIRC's way out. Typed ones too (Jinx's).

-- loop.mrc --
alias spin {
  var %i = 0
  while (1) inc %i
}
on *:TEXT:!spin:#:spin
on *:TEXT:!ping:#:msg # pong
-- transcript --
me trout
chan #trout trout bob
active #trout
/spin
= status: * script stopped: it ran more than 100000 steps (line 3, loop.mrc)
< :bob!b@h PRIVMSG #trout :!spin
= status: * script stopped: it ran more than 100000 steps (line 3, loop.mrc)
< :bob!b@h PRIVMSG #trout :!ping
> /msg #trout pong
//while (2 > 1) { noop }
= status: * script stopped: it ran more than 100000 steps
//while (1) { }
= status: * script stopped: it ran more than 100000 steps
